{"number":316,"title":"Canon patch (blocked on push scope): dedup-prune-integrity flags the VERSIONS.md row growth-dedup&#39;s own task doc mandates","body":"Working item #305 (`claudinite-growth/growth-dedup`) ran to completion — [PR #314](https://github.com/missingbulb/ClaudiniteWebsite/pull/314) merged, pruning two local rules the canon now covers — but the session&#39;s Stop-hook conformance gate then blocked on a check the growth-dedup task doc itself mandates tripping.

### What happened

`packs/claudinite-growth/tasks/growth-dedup/task.md` requires: *&#34;Every rule this run actually prunes gets a row at the top of its pack&#39;s `VERSIONS.md` table, in the same commit as the prune.&#34;* I added two rows to this repo&#39;s `.claudinite/local/packs/claudinite-website/VERSIONS.md` in the same commit as the prune, exactly as instructed.

That commit then failed `dedup-prune-integrity` (`packs/claudinite-growth/workRules/dedup-integrity.mjs`): its shrink invariant treats **every** `.md` file under a local pack as &#34;prose that must never grow&#34; in a dedup-labeled commit, with no exemption for `VERSIONS.md`. But `VERSIONS.md` is the pack&#39;s changelog — by the task doc&#39;s own convention it is *supposed* to grow by exactly one row per prune, in the very commit the shrink invariant is scoped to. The two rules are in direct conflict: following the task doc&#39;s mandatory VERSIONS.md step is what makes the backstop check fire.

(This didn&#39;t block CI on PR #314, because `check_the_world.mjs` — what CI runs — explicitly excludes `scope: &#39;work&#39;` rules; `dedup-prune-integrity` only runs via the session&#39;s own Stop hook, `check_the_work.mjs`. So the PR merged clean, and the conflict only surfaced afterward, blocking the session&#39;s own end-of-turn gate.)

### The fix

Exempt a pack&#39;s own `VERSIONS.md` from the shrink invariant (rule 2) — it&#39;s the record, not the pack; only the pack&#39;s prose (`RULES.md`, a skill doc) is held to &#34;shrink, never grow&#34;. Left the canon-restatement fingerprint (rule 1) unscoped, unchanged.

**Verified before this was written:**
- `node --test packs/claudinite-growth/test/*.test.mjs` — `92 pass / 0 fail` (88 pre-existing + 4 new)
- Every new test confirmed to **fail against the unmodified source first** (2 of 4 failed, exactly the two exercising the VERSIONS.md exemption), then pass after the fix
- `node engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs` — `0 blocking` (88 pre-existing advisories, unchanged by this diff)

**Local commit:** `248afe11` — *dedup-prune-integrity: exempt a pack&#39;s own VERSIONS.md from the shrink invariant* (2 files, +66/−1)

This session cannot push it — the git proxy serves `missingbulb/Claudinite` for a fetch but `403`s a push, since this session&#39;s GitHub scope is `missingbulb/claudinitewebsite` alone (an organisation egress policy; see #59 for the same shape). Preserved here for a session with canon scope to apply.

## To apply

```sh
git checkout -b claude/dedup-versions-exempt
git apply canon-dedup-versions-exempt.patch
```

